# Keep Debian's Xorg server out of the image entirely.
#
# This has to be an archives/*.pref.chroot rather than something 040-xlibre.chroot
# sets up, because live-build applies config/archives during chroot_prep -- before
# package lists install -- whereas hooks run afterwards. Without it, xinit
# (desktop.list.chroot) Recommends xserver-xorg, live-build installs Recommends,
# and the Xorg server lands during package installation only to be torn back out
# when the hook installs XLibre, which Conflicts with it. Blocking it up front
# skips the install-then-remove churn and makes the result deterministic.
#
# Nothing is lost: xserver-xlibre-core Provides xserver-xorg-core, so anything
# depending on the Xorg server is satisfied by XLibre instead. The negative pin
# applies to these package names only and does not affect the XLibre packages
# that provide them.
Package: xserver-xorg xserver-xorg-core
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1
